# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# Production values are set as environment variables on the host, not in a file.

# --- Server ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000

# --- Database ---
#
# Two roles, deliberately.
#
# DATABASE_URL is what the running application connects as: a least-privilege
# role that can read and write the working tables but can only INSERT into
# loan_events — no UPDATE, no DELETE, no TRUNCATE. That is what makes the
# append-only history a privilege rather than only a trigger.
#
# ADMIN_DATABASE_URL owns the schema and is used for migrations, seeding and the
# test harness reset. It is never used to serve a request.
#
# Both match docker-compose.yml (host port 5433).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://lending_app:lending_app_dev_password@localhost:5433/lending_library?schema=public"
ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://lending:lending_dev_password@localhost:5433/lending_library?schema=public"

# The integration suite talks to its own database, which it truncates between
# tests, so it must never point at data you care about. Same two-role split.
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://lending_app:lending_app_dev_password@localhost:5433/lending_library_test?schema=public"
TEST_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://lending:lending_dev_password@localhost:5433/lending_library_test?schema=public"

# If a host only issues a single database role, point ADMIN_DATABASE_URL at the
# same connection string as DATABASE_URL. The application still works and the
# append-only trigger still holds, but the privilege-level guarantee is gone.

# --- Auth ---
# Signs the session cookie. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# The server refuses to start in production if this is missing or left as the
# development placeholder.
SESSION_SECRET="dev-only-insecure-secret-change-me"

# --- Web (build-time, Vite) ---
# The SPA reads no environment variables at all. The API is same-origin in both
# development (proxied by the Vite dev server) and production (served by the same
# Node process), so relative /api paths work unchanged and there is no base URL
# to configure. web/vite.config.ts deliberately does not load this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production (Render + Neon)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these on the host, never in a file. render.yaml declares them; the two
# connection strings are marked `sync: false` so they are entered by hand.
#
#   NODE_ENV=production
#   SESSION_SECRET      generated by Render, 32+ random bytes
#
#   DATABASE_URL        Neon POOLED endpoint, as the least-privilege role:
#                       postgresql://lending_app:...@ep-xxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/lending_library
#                         ?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1
#
#   ADMIN_DATABASE_URL  Neon DIRECT endpoint, as the owner role:
#                       postgresql://OWNER:...@ep-xxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/lending_library
#                         ?sslmode=require
#
# Why two endpoints as well as two roles: migrations issue DDL, which cannot go
# through pgbouncer, so ADMIN_DATABASE_URL must be the direct endpoint. That
# happens to line up exactly with the privilege split already in place — the
# owner migrates, the restricted role serves requests.
#
# If the host only offers one role, set ADMIN_DATABASE_URL to the same value as
# DATABASE_URL. The application still works and the append-only trigger still
# holds, but the privilege-level guarantee on loan_events is gone. Say so in
# SUBMISSION.md rather than letting it pass unnoticed.
#
# One-off, after the first deploy, to load demo data:
#   ALLOW_PRODUCTION_SEED=true npm run db:seed

